  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(a) For ideal gas,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;functions of temperature&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>RT</mi></math>&nbsp;where f is total degree of freedom.&nbsp;</p><p>(b)&nbsp;Compressibility factor (Z) is equal to 1 for ideal gas.</p><p>(c)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#8722;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;</p><p>(d)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></msub><mi>dT</mi></math>&nbsp;for all processes</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
